### Step 1: Summary of Key Insights
The retrieved evidence presents contradictory accounts regarding the terrorist designation of the National Democratic Front (NDF). On one hand, a fact-check by Vera Files and an official UK Home Office document support the claim, showing that the United States, United Kingdom, Australia, and New Zealand designate the CPP-NPA but do not include the NDF on their official terrorist lists. On the other hand, a report from the Philippine News Agency (PNA) refutes the claim, stating that the "CPP-NPA-NDF" is collectively listed as a terrorist organization by the European Union, United States, United Kingdom, Australia, Canada, and New Zealand. Because the record contains clear but directly opposing evidence from these sources, no further investigation of the record is required to establish this contradiction.

---

### Step 3: Conclusion
Based on the recorded evidence, there is a direct contradiction between the sources. While independent fact-checking and official UK government documents indicate that the NDF is excluded from the terrorist lists of the US, UK, Australia, and New Zealand, a Philippine government news report asserts that the NDF is indeed included in the terrorist designations of these countries as well as the European Union. Because there is active documentation supporting and refuting the claim within the record, the final decision is `conflicting evidence`.

### Verdict: CONFLICTING

### Justification
The record presents conflicting evidence regarding the terrorist designation of the National Democratic Front (NDF). A fact-check by [Vera Files](https://verafiles.org/articles/vera-files-fact-check-badoy-errs-claiming-ndf-tagged-terror) and an official document from the [UK Home Office](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/266038/List_of_Proscribed_organisations.pdf) support the assertion that the United States, United Kingdom, Australia, and New Zealand exclude the NDF from their official terrorist lists, designating only the CPP-NPA. Conversely, a report by the [Philippine News Agency](https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1105350) contradicts this by stating that the European Union, United States, United Kingdom, Australia, Canada, and New Zealand collectively list the "CPP-NPA-NDF" as a terrorist organization.